Column name: usa_atcf_id Type: TEXT Description: The ATCF ID is assigned by US agencies and can be used to comparethe storm with other US cyclone-related datasets. If two (or more) ATCF tracks make up one storm/nthen the IDs are separated by a colon. The format of the ATCF ID is B<bb><nn><yyyy> where bb is the basin ID/nnn is the number of the storm in that basin and yyyy is the year. Possible basin values are: AL: North Atlantic/nSL: South Atlantic/nEP: East Pacific/nWP: West Pacific/nSH: Southern Hemisphere/nIO: North Indian For the provisional data/nother basin identifiers were provided that include: CP: Central Pacific/nSP: South Pacific/nSI: South Indian/nAS: Arabian Sea (North Indian) and BB: Bay of Bengal (North Indian)
